00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:42,000
Harry Charles Salusbury Lloyd is an English actor.

7
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:58,000
His performance in the Channel 4 miniseries The Fear (2012) earned
him a British Academy Television Award nomination.

8
00:50:08,000 --> 00:50:14,000
He gained prominence through his roles as Will Scarlet in the BBC drama Robin Hood (2006), Jeremy Baines in the Doctor Who episodes "Human
Nature" and "The Family of Blood" (2007), and Viserys Targaryen in the first season of the HBO series Game of Thrones (2011).

9
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:30,000
Lloyd played Paul Crosley in the WGN series Manhattan (2014), Peter Quayle in the Starz series
Counterpart (2017–2019), and Bernard Marx in the Peacock series Brave New World (2020).

10
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
He voiced Viktor in the Netflix animated series Arcane (2021–2024), Z in
Xenoblade Chronicles 3 (2022), and Ultima in Final Fantasy XVI (2023).

11
01:08:56,000 --> 01:09:02,000
He also appeared in Wolf Hall (2015) on BBC Two, series 1 of Marcella (2016) on ITV,
and the third season of the FX series Legion (2019) as Charles Xavier.

12
01:15:12,000 --> 01:15:18,000
Lloyd is also known for his theatre work, earning
an Off West End Award nomination.

13
01:21:28,000 --> 01:21:34,000
His films include The Theory of Everything (2014),
Anthropoid (2016), and The Wife (2017).

